# The Python packages the app installs, which go run ./cmd/divbast-pins
# locks into requirements.lock, with each file's sha256. The demo needs
# none. An app lists its own here, one a line, pinned with == or not, with
# any environment marker. An app built from an upstream that ships a
# requirements.txt names that file here alone instead, by one -r line, at
# the commit its Containerfile builds, as an ARG:
#
#   -r https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<owner>/<app>/${APP_COMMIT}/requirements.txt
#
# Nothing resolves dependencies: every package the image installs is named
# here, or in pins.txt, and pip check fails the build on one that is not.
